From: Gabriel Duarte Guerra <72227489+GabriWar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: guard against NULL entries in ttm->pages during
 unpopulate

amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate() walks ttm->pages[] and writes pages[i]->mapping
without checking for NULL. If a GPU command fails partway through, the buffer
object can be left partially populated and cleanup dereferences a NULL page:

  RIP: 0010:amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate+0x77/0xd0 [amdgpu]
  CR2: 0000000000000018
  RAX: 0000000000000000  RBX: ffff8c72d0b6e180  RCX: 0000000000000000
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception

CR2 = 0x18 is the offset of struct page::mapping, confirming pages[i] was NULL.

This matters on the BC-250 because GPU command failures on gfx1013 are routine
while the compute defect is unresolved, and every one of them risked taking the
whole blade down -- four hard hangs in a single debugging session upstream, with
unclean shutdowns and filesystem data loss. With the guard the failing process
still dies but the machine survives.

This addresses the crash, not the reason a BO ends up partially populated. It
is a containment patch: it keeps a fault survivable so the defect can be
investigated with patch 17 instead of rebooting the blade. The missing NULL
check is upstream code, not distro-specific, and is worth upstreaming
independently of the BC-250.

Originally authored and tested by Gabriel Duarte Guerra against a full Stable
Diffusion pipeline on gfx1013; carried here unmodified in substance, with the
comment reworded. Source:
http://192.168.40.16:3000/nightcarnage/bc250-rocm-gabriwar
patches/0001-drm-amdgpu-guard-against-NULL-pages.patch

Signed-off-by: Gabriel Duarte Guerra <72227489+GabriWar@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
@@ -1168,8 +1168,13 @@
 	if (ttm->page_flags & TTM_TT_FLAG_EXTERNAL)
 		return;
 
+	/* A BO left partially populated by an aborted GPU command has NULL
+	 * holes in pages[]; without this the cleanup path panics on
+	 * NULL->mapping (CR2=0x18). Fixes the crash, not the abort.
+	 */
 	for (i = 0; i < ttm->num_pages; ++i)
-		ttm->pages[i]->mapping = NULL;
+		if (ttm->pages[i])
+			ttm->pages[i]->mapping = NULL;
 
 	adev = amdgpu_ttm_adev(bdev);
 
